  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Lord is a man of war, Ex. 15:3. noise of war in the camp, Ex. 32:17. book of the wars of the Lord, Num. 21:14. warred against the Midianites, Num. 31:7. new wife, he shall not go out to war, Deut. 24:5. land rested from war, Josh. 11:23. weapons of war perished, 2 Sam. 1:27. He teacheth my hands to war, 2 Sam. 22:35 (Ps. 18:34; 144:1). war between Rehoboam and Jeroboam, 1 Kgs. 14:30 (15:6; 2 Chr. 12:15). up to Jerusalem to war, 2 Kgs. 16:5 (Isa. 7:1). though war should rise against me, Ps. 27:3. maketh wars to cease, Ps. 46:9. scatter thou the people that delight in war, Ps. 68:30. with good advice make war, Prov. 20:18. by wise counsel thou shalt make thy war, Prov. 24:6. time of war, and a time of peace, Eccl. 3:8. neither shall they learn war any more, Isa. 2:4 (Micah 4:3; 2 Ne. 12:4). they fled … from the grievousness of war, Isa. 21:15. they that war against thee shall be as nothing, Isa. 41:12. set in array as men for war against thee, Jer. 6:23. Egypt, where we shall see no war, Jer. 42:14. same horn made war with the saints, Dan. 7:21 (Rev. 13:7). Proclaim ye this among the Gentiles; Prepare war, Joel 3:9. pass by securely as men averse from war, Micah 2:8.",
